.Dd October 15, 2026
.Dt WSD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm wsd
.Nd window server and compositor speaking the SkyLight WindowServer protocol
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl S
.Op Fl t
.Op Fl b Ar backend
.Op Fl r Ar renderer
.Op Fl g Ar WxH
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Op Fl c Ar card
.Op Fl n Ar rendernode
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a window server for FreeBSD that implements the wire protocol of the macOS WindowServer
(the SkyLight MIG subsystems), composes the windows of its clients with shadows, rounded
corners, alpha and background blur, and routes keyboard, pointer and scroll input to them.
It listens on a stream socket (SOCK_SEQPACKET) that only its own user can open.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width "-n rendernode"
.It Fl b Ar backend
.Cm headless
(default) or
.Cm kms
(DRM/KMS display and evdev input, built with
.Ql gmake kms ) .
.It Fl r Ar renderer
.Cm sw
(default, CPU) or
.Cm gl
(OpenGL ES 2 through EGL, built with
.Ql gmake gl ) .
.It Fl g Ar WxH
Screen size of the headless backend (default 1280x800).
.It Fl s Ar socket
Socket path.
Default:
.Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR Ns /wsd.sock ,
else
.Pa /tmp/wsd- Ns Ar uid Ns Pa .sock .
.It Fl S
Enter Capsicum capability mode once the server is set up.
.It Fl t
Test mode: enables the private requests used by the test suite (screenshot to a file,
input injection, quit).
Never use it on a session that matters.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
.It Ev WS_SOCKET
Socket path used by clients and by
.Nm
when
.Fl s
is not given.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "%%PREFIX%%/etc/rc.d/wsd"
.It Pa %%PREFIX%%/etc/rc.d/wsd
rc(8) script, see its header for the rc.conf variables.
.It Pa %%PREFIX%%/bin/wsstart
Starts a private server for the current user and runs a client on it.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr capsicum 4 ,
.Xr rc.conf 5
.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
Connections from other users are refused, each connection is limited in windows,
buffers, surfaces and memory, and with
.Fl S
the process cannot open new files after start-up.
